    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      68.48,
      695.81,
      427.79,
      713.69
    ],
    "text": "favour of the Respondent. This appeal is from the said judgment.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.399999618530273,
      13.923715591430664
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      294.12,
      71.26,
      301.99,
      85.27
    ],
    "text": "3",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.5
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      137.25,
      105.44,
      529.15,
      123.58
    ],
    "text": "At the outset I must place on record that where no malicious or",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.600000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      68.04,
      129.18,
      528.59,
      147.33
    ],
    "text": "corrupt motive in prosecuting an action was alleged or proved, no action for",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.600000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      67.81,
      152.94,
      528.29,
      171.09
    ],
    "text": "damages will lie, even though inconvenience and pecuniary loss have been caused.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.600000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      67.85,
      176.7,
      528.83,
      194.85
    ],
    "text": "In an action for a malicious prosecution the plaintiff must prove that the charge",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.600000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      67.9,
      200.23,
      528.91,
      218.38
    ],
    "text": "must have been false, there must have been wanting of probable cause to justify the",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.600000381469727,
      14.027238845825195
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      68.02,
      224.0,
      530.83,
      242.14
    ],
    "text": "accusation, there have been malice on the part of the informant, and the plaintiff",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.600000381469727,
      14.027238845825195
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      68.12,
      247.51,
      526.19,
      265.66
    ],
    "text": "must have sustained damage either in his person or reputation or by pecuniary loss.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.578283309936523,
      13.600000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      137.67,
      284.71,
      529.35,
      302.85
    ],
    "text": "Lascelles ACJ in Corea Vs Peiris 9 NLR 276 stated that \"the",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.600000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      68.26,
      308.46,
      528.75,
      326.61
    ],
    "text": "conditions which are necessary to success in an action of malicious prosecution are",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.578283309936523,
      13.600000381469727,
      14.027238845825195
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      68.53,
      332.24,
      529.18,
      350.38
    ],
    "text": "laid down as follows by Lord Justice Bowen in Abrath v. North-Eastern Railway",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.221842765808105,
      13.517802238464355,
      13.600000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      68.26,
      355.99,
      529.12,
      374.13
    ],
    "text": "Co. (1883)11 Q.B.D. 440. In order to establish his cause of action it is incumbent",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.595549583435059,
      13.600000381469727,
      14.161460876464844
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      68.4,
      379.52,
      529.07,
      397.66
    ],
    "text": "upon the plaintiff to prove - (1) that he was innocent, and that his innocence was",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.600000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      68.41,
      403.26,
      529.46,
      421.41
    ],
    "text": "pronounced by the tribunal before which the accusation was made; (2) that there",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.600000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      68.37,
      427.04,
      529.03,
      445.18
    ],
    "text": "was a want of reasonable and probable cause for the prosecution, or, as it may",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.517802238464355,
      13.600000381469727,
      14.027238845825195
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      68.75,
      450.8,
      529.38,
      468.94
    ],
    "text": "otherwise be stated, that the circumstances of the case were such as to be in the",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.600000381469727,
      14.027238845825195
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      68.48,
      474.31,
      529.05,
      492.46
    ],
    "text": "eyes of the Judge inconsistent with the existence of reasonable and probable cause;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.600000381469727,
      14.027238845825195
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      68.73,
      498.08,
      529.0,
      516.22
    ],
    "text": "(3) that the proceedings of which he complains were initiated in a malicious spirit,",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.600000381469727,
      14.161460876464844
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      68.37,
      521.59,
      503.57,
      539.74
    ],
    "text": "that is, from an indirect and improper motive, and not in furtherance of justice.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.596449851989746,
      13.600000381469727,
      13.891721725463867
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      138.37,
      559.27,
      530.1,
      577.42
    ],
    "text": "In the case of Silva Vs Silva [2002] 2 S.L.R. 29 it was held that \"In a",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.600000381469727,
      14.027238845825195
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      68.99,
      582.78,
      529.79,
      600.93
    ],
    "text": "case of malicious prosecution the onus of proof is on the plaintiff, he must prove",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.600000381469727,
      13.891721725463867,
      14.027238845825195
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      69.23,
      606.3,
      447.37,
      624.45
    ],
    "text": "on a preponderance of evidence or on a balance of probabilities that;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.600000381469727,
      14.161460876464844
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      86.17,
      643.51,
      401.04,
